Package: climgrain
Title: Temporal Climate Resolution for Ecological Prediction
Version: 0.3.0
Authors@R:
    person("Gilles", "Colling", email = "gilles.colling051@gmail.com",
           role = c("aut", "cre", "cph"),
           comment = c(ORCID = "0000-0003-3070-6066"))
Description: Builds model-ready representations of climate records at a
    chosen temporal grain, from the unreduced record down to a single value
    per year, and locates the grain at which predictive skill saturates.
    Calendar-aware binning keeps a bin a real week or month rather than a
    fixed block of hours, and a window can be summarised by its mean, by its
    extreme readings, or by its coldest and warmest day. The default response
    is presence-absence with a joint multi-label head scored by the true skill
    statistic, the setting used for species distribution modelling from
    microclimate loggers, and both the response head and the metric are
    registered rather than hard-coded.
